  "narration": {
    "pattern_romaji": "A wa nan / doko / dare desu ka",
    "pattern_jp": "Aは なん／どこ／だれ ですか",
    "pattern_english": "What / where / who is A?",
    "slots": [
      {
        "slot": "A",
        "fits": "the topic you're asking about: a thing, place, or person (トイレ, あれ, このかさ, えき)"
      },
      {
        "slot": "question word",
        "fits": "なん (what), どこ (where), or だれ (who). It goes exactly where the answer will go. Add の for 'whose' (だれの) or 'what kind of' (なんの)"
      }
    ],
    "segments": [
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Welcome back! Today's pattern is {Aはなんですか}. It means: What is A?"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "And it has two cousins: {Aはどこですか}, Where is A? And {Aはだれですか}, Who is A?"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Here's the big secret. Japanese doesn't move question words to the front like English does. The question word sits right where the answer will go."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "You already know {AはBです}, A is B. To ask a question, just drop a question word into the B slot and finish with {ですか}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "So: {なん} means what. {どこ} means where. {だれ} means who. And {ですか} still comes last, turning it into a question."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Let's build one you'll really need. Start with the topic."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "トイレ"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Toilet. Now add the topic marker {は}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "トイレは"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "As for the toilet. Now put the question word in the answer slot."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "トイレはどこ"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "As for the toilet, where. Finish with {ですか}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "トイレはどこですか。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Where is the toilet? And the answer simply replaces {どこ}:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "トイレはあれです。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "The toilet is that one over there. Same skeleton, answer dropped into the same slot."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Second one. Start with that thing over there, {あれ}, add {は}, then {なん}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "あれは"
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "あれはなん"
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "あれはなんですか。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "What is that over there?"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Third. Start with {このかさ}, this umbrella. Add {は}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "このかさは"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "As for this umbrella. Now remember {の}, the word for 's? Stick it on {だれ}, and {だれの} means whose."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "このかさはだれのかさ"
